{"name":"Divine Inspiration","hex":"#d8e2e1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"divine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to a god.","Eternal, holy, or otherwise godlike."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One skilled in divinity; a theologian.","A minister of the gospel; a priest; a clergyman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/divine"},{"term":"inspiration","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The drawing of air into the lungs, accomplished in mammals by elevation of the chest walls and flattening of the diaphragm, as part of the act of breathing.","A single inward breath (intake of air)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/inspiration"}],"entries":[{"title":"Divine inspiration","blocks":[{"text":"Divine inspiration is the concept of a supernatural force, typically a deity, causing a person or people to experience a creative desire. It has been a commonly reported aspect of many religions, for thousands of years. Divine inspiration is often closely tied to the concept of revelation, information being revealed or disclosed through communication with a deity or other supernatural entity or entities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divine_inspiration"},{"title":"Divine Inspiration (RuPaul's Drag Race)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Divine Inspiration\" is the ninth episode of the seventh season of RuPaul's Drag Race. Directed by Nick Murray, the episode originally aired on April 27, 2015. Demi Lovato and John Waters are guest judges. Lucian Piane and Our Lady J also make guest appearances, helping the contestants during rehearsals."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divine_Inspiration_(RuPaul's_Drag_Race)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Pink_Flamingos_trailer_screenshot_%282%29.jpg/500px-Pink_Flamingos_trailer_screenshot_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https:/